		(uuid "5d7c3a60-9dc2-a838-eca4-0c8e0c316967")
	)
	(text_box "IEEE-488 plug, hand-\nsoldered. Contacts\n1-12 run along the\nwide side of the D.\nTTL levels, low =\ntrue, 0 to 5.5 V; the\ndrivers sink 48 mA and\nthe terminations are\ninside U2 and U3.\nConnect only to an\nIEEE-488 bus."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 382.27 88.9 0)
		(size 22.86 21.59)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6333938a-25ac-e46e-8260-c741703613ef")
	)
	(text_box "An RP2354A runs the IEEE-488 handshake and talks to the host\nover USB as a Prologix-compatible serial controller (and, in a\nlater firmware, a USBTMC/USB488 instrument). Two TI transceivers\n(SN75160B data, SN75161B control) drive the bus as IEEE 488.1\nasks: 48 mA sinks, terminations, hysteresis, and no load on the\nbus when unpowered. Their 5 V is switched on by the firmware\nonce the host has configured the USB port, so the board is off\nthe bus until the firmware is ready. The plug hangs under the\nboard; everything else is on top."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 238.76 0)
